  "rationale": "The acquire tradition hook now reaches a running universe, so the reference universe's costs are its tradition's rather than the catalog's authored ones. applyAcquire had no caller outside a test: the world loop priced research against the authored researchCost, gated teaching on the authored teachCost, and created every derived instance at the placeholder mastery, so one of the four hooks vision.md 4a licenses was inert. The reference universe resolves to True Naming -- scribingTraditionId picks the first tradition whose store keeps written copies, and interning is code-unit order -- which declares 2x research, 0.5x teaching and full mastery on arrival. Research therefore costs twice what it did, which is the whole of the movement here: nodesGained 30.15 to 18.93, nodesKnown 32.65 to 21.43, knowledgeInstances 445.14 to 369.83, grimoires 116.70 to 97.05, libraryDepth 1.71 to 1.47. Population is untouched to two decimals, as it should be -- acquire says nothing about demography. Teaching now happens at all, where before every mage sat below TEACH_THRESHOLD forever; it does not show as a separate metric because none is collected. This is a defect fix, not a tuning change: no magnitude moved, and every one of them is still untuned. These numbers are a measurement and not a balance claim -- release-plan.md forbids any balance claim before 0.5.0 -- and they still describe a universe degenerate in known ways: all 200 runs are the passive control, which submits no god verb, so no strategy is exercised; and library depth stays near 1.5 distinct nodes against a hundred-odd grimoires, because the scribable list is cost-ordered and the same cheap nodes are copied over and over.",
